IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `bgg3-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-nouns`
IMPORT `bgg4-seams`

-- bgg4-tests-seams: tests for the seams between chapter 3 and chapter 4.  Expected values are written from the text
-- (quoted beside the assertion) and from the chapter 3 text each call stands for, not from the code's output.


§ `Art 77(2) of chapter 3: the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands, or not`

-- Chapter 3 Art 77(2): "Die Artikel 48 Absatz 3, 90-98, 103 Absatz 2, 105 Absatz 2, 106 Absatz 1 sowie 107 Absatz 2, soweit dieser dem Bundesgericht erlaubt, in der Sache selbst zu entscheiden, sind in diesen Fällen nicht anwendbar."
-- Art 95 is within 90-98: not applicable, so the chapter 4 answer is not an answer
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 95 0 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 90 is within 90-98
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 90 0 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 98 is within 90-98, a chapter 4 JUST FALSE is not an answer either
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 98 0 FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 99 is not in the list: the chapter 4 answer stands
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 99 0 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Art 103(1) is not in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 103 1 FALSE (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Art 103(2) is in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 103 2 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 105(2) is in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 105 2 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 105(1) is not in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 105 1 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Art 106(1) is in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 106 1 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 106(2) is not in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 106 2 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Art 107(2) so far as it lets the Court decide the matter itself
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 107 2 TRUE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 107(2) outside that part is not in the list
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` TRUE 107 2 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not an arbitral award appeal: the paragraph does not reach it
#ASSERT `Art 77(2) the answer of a chapter 4 provision stands for the appeal` FALSE 95 0 FALSE (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Art 111(1) and the standing of chapter 3`

-- kind, tookPart, hadNoChance, especiallyAffected, interest, person, detentionDecision, civilClaimsAffected, complaintRightAsSuch, legallyProtectedInterest
-- civil, Art 76(1): took part before the lower instance, and especially affected, and an interest worthy of protection
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- criminal, Art 81(1)(b)(1): the accused person has a legally protected interest
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` `appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE `accused person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- public law, Art 89(1)
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` `appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- another kind of appeal: chapter 3 gives no standing
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) the person is entitled to appeal, by chapter 3` `another kind of appeal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Art 111(1): the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party; anyone else is not reached
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) with chapter 3 the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) with chapter 3 the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 111(1) with chapter 3 the person entitled to appeal must be able to take part as a party before all cantonal lower instances` `another kind of appeal` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE `another person` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 110 and the cantons' duties of chapter 3`

-- Art 75(2), 80(2): "Die Kantone setzen als letzte kantonale Instanzen obere Gerichte ein"; Art 86(2), (3) for public law
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` `appeal in public-law matters` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 110 the canton must set up a court as last cantonal instance under chapter 3` `another kind of appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- kind, political character, freely reviews the facts, applies the law of its own motion
#ASSERT `Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` `appeal in public-law matters` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 110 with chapter 3 the canton has ensured the review by a judicial authority` `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Art 112(1)(d) and the value limits of chapter 3`

-- kind, pecuniary, employment, tenancy, state liability, public-law employment
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in civil matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in public-law matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `appeal in criminal matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) chapter 3 provides a value limit for the appeal` `another kind of appeal` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- kind, pecuniary, employment, tenancy, state liability, public employment, subject to appeal, notice, states value
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a limit exists, the value is not stated: the decision falls short
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- no notice at all: short on either reading
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in civil matters` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- chapter 3 does not settle whether a limit exists (criminal): the answer stands only if it is the same both ways
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not subject to appeal: the paragraph does not reach it
#ASSERT `Art 112(1)(d) with chapter 3 the decision contains a notice of legal remedies including the value in dispute where the Act provides a value limit` `appeal in criminal matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Art 109(1) and the conditions of Art 74 and 83 to 85`

-- legal assistance field, subject, elementary principles violated, serious defects abroad, particularly important for other reasons,
-- tax assistance field, fundamental question, pecuniary, state liability, public-law employment, value in francs,
-- kind of appeal, employment law case, tenancy law case, single cantonal instance, cantonal supervisory authority, bankruptcy and composition judge,
-- deciding body.  The first eleven inputs are the old ones; every assertion below that was written before the Art 74 seam gives the public-law kind
-- and no Art 74 fact, so its expected value is the one it always had.
-- Art 84(1): "nur zulässig, wenn er eine Auslieferung ... betrifft und es sich um einen besonders bedeutenden Fall handelt"
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` TRUE `extradition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS `only if the case is a particularly important case`
-- Art 84a: "wenn sich eine Rechtsfrage von grundsätzlicher Bedeutung stellt oder wenn es sich aus anderen Gründen um einen besonders bedeutenden Fall im Sinne von Artikel 84 Absatz 2 handelt"
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` FALSE `another subject` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises or the case is a particularly important case`
-- Art 85(1), (2): value below the limit in state liability
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` FALSE `another subject` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 20000 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises`
-- Art 85(1)(b): value below 15 000 francs in public-law employment
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` FALSE `another subject` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE 10000 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS `only if a legal question of fundamental importance arises`
-- value at or above the limit: no condition applies
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` FALSE `another subject` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE 40000 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS `on neither of these conditions`
-- nothing engaged
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) the condition on which the appeal is admissible, by chapters 3` FALSE `another subject` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS `on neither of these conditions`
-- the bench of three: only where neither condition is present
#ASSERT `Art 109(1) with chapter 3 the division decides in a bench of three on non-entry` TRUE `extradition` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE 0 `appeal in public-law matters` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `another body` EQUALS JUST TRUE
